From fbf0a82fd70a92963cb2dcea10ae93d660e27b64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:13:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [MOS] Extract opt-in native widths and near-memory
 prerequisites

Extract the native compiler support tracked by #321 from the downstream aggregate, excluding far address spaces and platform code. Reconcile current scalarization, byte-mode behavior and native DWARF numbering. Include byte-index, wide-anyext, immediate-width and near atomic guards needed by this compiler subset. Existing implementation credits and dated evidence remain in llvm-mos-65816 records.

Extraction assistance: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.158.0 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0e75a-a9ed-7372-9bac-b19b732a46a2.
